-- title:
--   Normality from regularity at non-maximal primes and depth two
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$ be a Noetherian integrally closed domain with fraction field $K_0$, and let $B$ be a Noetherian local ring which is a module-finite $R_0$-algebra with $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} B \le 2$. Let $F$ be a commutative ring carrying compatible $B$-, $R_0$- and $K_0$-algebra structures (the two scalar towers $R_0 \to B \to F$ and $R_0 \to K_0 \to F$), and assume $F$ is the localisation of $B$ at the submonoid generated by the image of the non-zero-divisors of $R_0$, that $\operatorname{algebraMap} B F$ is injective, that $F$ is reduced, and that $F$ is separable over $K_0$. Assume further that for every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ which is not maximal the localisation $B_{\mathfrak p}$ is a regular local ring, and that there are elements $a, b \in B$ forming a regular sequence (in the sense of `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular`) on $B$. Then $B$ is a domain, $B$ is integrally closed in its fraction field, $F$ is a field, and $F$ is a fraction field of $B$.
--
--   This is the normality criterion for the generic fibre of a module-finite algebra over a normal Noetherian base: regularity in codimension one together with a depth-two condition at the closed point yields a normal domain whose generic fibre is its fraction field, bypassing any appeal to excellence. It is used in the analysis of completed local rings of modular curves, in particular by the results on adic completions of module-finite algebras unramified outside the closed point and on the local structure of the crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_and_isFractionRing_of_forall_not_isMaximal_isRegularLocalRing.lean

